2) XGobi Background:

XGobi is a dynamical statistical graphics program, developed
by Debby Swayne, Di Cook, and Andreas Buja.

It supports one-dimensional plots, scatterplots, scatterplot matrizes,
parallel coordinate plots, the grand tour, linked brushing, and much more.
It also provides exploratory features that are useful for spatial data sets.

+ The XGobi home page is
   http://www.research.att.com/areas/stat/xgobi/

Many papers on the use of XGobi are available through this page.


+ A book on XGobi is currently in the making. Draft chapters are
available at
   http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dicook/xgobi-book/xgobi.html

Most useful for our class are the Introduction and the chapter on Space.


+ Additional publications how to use XGobi and ArcView/XGobi/XploRe
are available through my "Publications & Videos" Web page.

