5) Use of ArcView/XGobi:

Before starting:

Type "setenv" and check that the environment variable HOST is set to
the name of the machine you are currently using. If this is not the case,
type the command "setenv HOST currentmachinename", i.e., use the name
of the machine you are currently working at.

Start ArcView:
  arcview &

In the prompt, click on "Open an existing project", then "OK".
CD into /home/symanzik/axx/av_dir/av_data and select the file
"AV2XG_DEMO_UTall.apr" (and click OK).

Select "File", then "Extensions", activate the "ArcView XGobi link",
and click "OK". A new menu button "XGobi" will appear in the command
line.

Activate a theme, e.g., "Places", select "XGobi", then "Basic Link",
hit the "Green Diamond", chose a field for row labels in XGobi
(e.g., Name2), and click "OK". Then start brushing on either side...

To stop XGobi, click on the "Red Diamond". Always stop XGobi first,
then quit ArcView. In case that XGobi crashes or you save your project
with the current symbols visible in the ArcView map view, you can
select "Edit" and "Select All Graphics", followed by "Edit" and
"Cut Graphics" which removes the symbols from the map view.

If you made changes to this demo project and want to keep these
changes for a future session, you have to use the option
"File" and "Save Project As" and indicate a directory for which you 
have write permission. If you just try "File" and "Save Project",
you get the error message "ArcView cannot save or create this file" 
since you do not have write permission to my directories.

