7) XploRe is a statistical computing environment, developed at 
Humboldt University zu Berlin, Germany, that has been added as 
an analytical statistical package to the ArcView/XGobi link in 1997.

The main XploRe Web page is
  http://www.xplore-stat.de
and a US mirror is available at
  http://www.galaxy.gmu.edu/~xplore

In short, XploRe can be started from within XGobi and it contains
the spatial statistics functions described in Venables/Ripley (1999).
Thus, we have the link ArcView <-> XGobi <-> XploRe

A tutorial how to start XploRe from within XGobi and conduct 
linked brushing is available at
  http://www.xplore-stat.de/tutorials/rpcframe1.html
  http://www.galaxy.gmu.edu/~xplore/tutorials/rpcframe1.html

A tutorial on spatial statistics in XploRe is available at
  http://www.xplore-stat.de/tutorials/spatialframe1.html
  http://www.galaxy.gmu.edu/~xplore/tutorials/spatialframe1.html

To start XploRe from within XGobi, select "Tools" and "Start XploRe"
within XGobi. To select variables to be passed from XGobi to XploRe,
select "Tools" and "Variable List" and mark those variables with a "+"
you want to use in XploRe. Then select "File" and "XploRe (pass variables)"
to pass the data into XploRe. On the XploRe side, you can then access
the data from XGobi via the variable name XGobiData.

